problem:
Problem description
- There is a finite set of processing devices $$\mathcal{D}$$ and a finite planning horizon $$\mathcal{T}$$.
- There is a finite set of products $$\mathcal{P}$$; the original instance contains a single product, but the model is written in generalized indexed form.
- For each device $$d \in \mathcal{D}$$, the fixed preparation completion cost is $$F_d$$, the unit production cost for product $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$ on that device is $$C_{d,p}$$, and the maximum processing capacity is $$U_d$$.
- The required demand for each product $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$ over the planning horizon is given by $$Q_p$$.
- The decision is to choose which devices to enable and how much of each product to assign to each enabled device.
- Production may be split across multiple devices as long as all demand is met and no device exceeds its capacity.
- A device that is not enabled cannot produce any quantity.
- If a device is enabled, its fixed preparation completion cost is incurred once.
- The planning goal is to minimize the total cost made up of device enabling costs and unit production costs while satisfying all demand.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$y_d$$, a binary decision variable indicating whether device $$d$$ is enabled.
  - $$x_{d,p}$$, a nonnegative decision variable giving the quantity of product $$p$$ produced on device $$d$$.
  - $$Z$$, the total minimized cost of the plan.

Input Format
{
  "devices": "$$\mathcal{D}$$, indexed by $$d \in \mathcal{D}$$",
  "products": "$$\mathcal{P}$$, indexed by $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$",
  "planning_horizon": "$$\mathcal{T}$$",
  "demand": "$$Q_p$$, a vector of length $$|\mathcal{P}|$$ giving required quantity for each product $$p$$ over $$\mathcal{T}$$",
  "setup_cost": "$$F_d$$, a vector of length $$|\mathcal{D}|$$ giving fixed enabling cost for each device $$d$$",
  "unit_production_cost": "$$C_{d,p}$$, a matrix of shape $$|\mathcal{D}|\\times|\mathcal{P}|$$ giving unit cost for producing product $$p$$ on device $$d$$",
  "capacity": "$$U_d$$, a vector of length $$|\mathcal{D}|$$ giving maximum processing capacity for each device $$d$$"
}

Output Format
{
  "enabled_devices": "list of devices $$d \\in \\mathcal{D}$$ with $$y_d = 1$$",
  "production_plan": "$$x_{d,p}$$, a matrix of shape $$|\mathcal{D}|\\times|\mathcal{P}|$$ giving production quantities assigned to each device-product pair",
  "total_cost": "$$Z^*$$, the minimum total cost"
}

Example(s)

